      "writtenOn": "2020-03-16T13:42:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Per IM conversation: I thought the purpose of mActiveTetheringRequests was to track the latest request for each tethering type, so that the following happens:\n\n1. startTethering with IP address X\n2. time passes.\n3. startTethering with IP address Y\n\nThen #3 would stop the downstream and restart it.\n\nBut I now see that it\u0027s just used locally for the time between the call to startTethering (which asks the downstream to start) and the time when the downstream actually calls back and we start IpServer.\n\nThat said, it would be good to support changing the configuration though. Maybe we could do it with something like this?\n\n    private static class TetheringRequestInfo {\n        TetheringRequestParcel request;\n        boolean isActive;  // true iff this request is currently active, i.e., being served by IpServer\n    }\n\nWe could add one of these in startTethering with isActive \u003d false, and then set isActive to true when we actually start the IpServer. Then, if someone later calls startTethering, and there is an active configuration, we would stop IpServer and start it again.\n\nNot for this CL.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 501,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 507,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "b699a908e4f1f6e1376ab53eece4feb4dba5922c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
